\section{The Unpaywall client}

The client encapsulates the HTTP session, the per-DOI cache, proactive rate
limiting, and the contact email.  It is modelled on [[CrossrefClient]]; the
shared [[load_cache]]/[[register_cache]] calls give it its own
[[unpaywall.pkl]] next to the provider caches, so [[scholar cache info]] and
[[scholar cache clear]] cover it without further work.

The email is resolved on every request rather than once at construction.
The difference is invisible in normal use (environment lookups are cheap),
but it means a process that sets [[SCHOLAR_EMAIL]] after import---a test, or a
notebook---sees the change, and that [[is_configured]] always reflects the
current environment rather than the state at import time.

<<the unpaywall client>>=
class UnpaywallClient:
    """Looks up open-access locations for DOIs via Unpaywall."""

    name = "unpaywall"

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self._cache: dict = load_cache(self.name)
        register_cache(self.name, self._cache)
        self._last_request_time: float = 0.0
        self._session = self._create_session()
        self._warned_unconfigured = False

    @property
    def email(self) -> str | None:
        """The contact email sent with every request, or ``None``."""
        return contact_email()

    def is_configured(self) -> bool:
        """Whether a contact email is available (Unpaywall requires one)."""
        return bool(self.email)

    <<unpaywall client methods>>
@

The session carries the same exponential back-off as the other providers: an
OA lookup that trips a transient 429 or 5xx should retry quietly rather than
report a false \enquote{could not check}.

<<unpaywall client methods>>=
def _create_session(self) -> requests.Session:
    """Create a session with exponential back-off retry logic."""
    session = requests.Session()
    retry = Retry(
        total=3,
        backoff_factor=1,  # 1s, 2s, 4s delays
        status_forcelist=[429, 500, 502, 503, 504],
        allowed_methods=["GET"],
    )
    session.mount("https://", HTTPAdapter(max_retries=retry))
    return session
@

Unpaywall's stated limit is generous (100\,000 calls per day), but enriching a
large session issues one request per paper in a burst.  A short minimum
interval keeps us a polite neighbour without making a few dozen lookups feel
slow.

<<unpaywall client methods>>=
def _wait_for_rate_limit(self) -> None:
    """Ensure a minimum interval between Unpaywall requests."""
    elapsed = time.time() - self._last_request_time
    if elapsed < UNPAYWALL_MIN_INTERVAL:
        time.sleep(UNPAYWALL_MIN_INTERVAL - elapsed)
    self._last_request_time = time.time()
@

<<constants>>=
# Unpaywall REST endpoint for single-DOI lookups, and request tuning.
UNPAYWALL_URL = "https://api.unpaywall.org/v2"
UNPAYWALL_TIMEOUT = 30
UNPAYWALL_MIN_INTERVAL = 0.1  # seconds between requests (polite pacing)
UNPAYWALL_USER_AGENT = "scholarcli (https://github.com/dbosk/scholar)"
@

\subsection{Fetching a DOI's open-access record}

The lookup is the heart of the module.  The DOI is URL-encoded before it is
spliced into the path: DOIs routinely contain slashes and occasionally other
reserved characters, which would otherwise be read as extra path segments and
produce a spurious 404.

The return contract is the checked/unknown distinction from the overview: a
normalized dictionary when Unpaywall served the record (HTTP~200) and [[None]]
when it did not (missing DOI, unconfigured email, 404, 429, or error).  A 404
is cached as [[None]] so an unregistered DOI is not retried every run; a 429 or
transport error is left uncached so a later run can try again.  The
unconfigured case is logged once per process rather than once per paper, since
a session of fifty papers would otherwise produce fifty identical warnings.

<<unpaywall client methods>>=
def fetch_oa(self, doi: str | None) -> dict | None:
    """Return open-access metadata for ``doi``, or ``None`` if undetermined.

    On an HTTP 200 response, returns a dict with ``is_oa``, ``oa_status``,
    ``oa_url``, ``pdf_url``, ``host_type``, ``version`` and ``license``.
    Returns ``None`` when the DOI is missing, no contact email is
    configured, the DOI is not found, the request is rate-limited, or it
    fails.
    """
    if not doi:
        return None
    if not self.is_configured():
        if not self._warned_unconfigured:
            logger.warning(
                "unpaywall: no contact email configured; set SCHOLAR_EMAIL "
                "to enable open-access lookups"
            )
            self._warned_unconfigured = True
        return None

    cache_key = ("oa", doi)
    if cache_key in self._cache:
        logger.debug("unpaywall: cache hit for DOI %s", doi)
        return self._cache[cache_key]

    try:
        self._wait_for_rate_limit()
        url = f"{UNPAYWALL_URL}/{quote(doi, safe='')}"
        response = self._session.get(
            url,
            params={"email": self.email},
            headers={"User-Agent": UNPAYWALL_USER_AGENT},
            timeout=UNPAYWALL_TIMEOUT,
        )

        if response.status_code == 404:
            # DOI unknown to Unpaywall: cache the miss to avoid re-lookups.
            self._cache[cache_key] = None
            return None
        if response.status_code == 429:
            logger.warning("unpaywall: rate limited for DOI %s", doi)
            return None

        response.raise_for_status()
        result = _normalize_oa(response.json())
        self._cache[cache_key] = result
        return result

    except requests.exceptions.HTTPError as e:
        logger.warning("unpaywall: lookup error for %s: %s", doi, e)
        return None
    except Exception as e:
        logger.warning("unpaywall: lookup failed for %s: %s", doi, e)
        return None
@

Let's verify the happy path, the email precondition, the encoding
requirement, and each \enquote{undetermined} branch.  We mock the session's
