\section{Normalizing the Unpaywall record}

Unpaywall's DOI object is large (authors, journal identifiers, every
location) and its shape is theirs to change; we flatten the few fields the rest
of the system needs into a small, stable dictionary so nothing outside this
chapter has to know the wire format.

Two choices deserve a word.  First, the PDF link prefers
[[best_oa_location.url_for_pdf]] but falls back to the first location that
has one: Unpaywall ranks the \emph{best copy} (publisher version first), and
that copy sometimes has only a landing page while a repository copy further
down has a direct PDF---for the reader who wants the file, a second-best
version with a link beats the best version without one.  Second, [[oa_url]] is
the best location's [[url]], falling back to its landing page: it is the
address to send a human to, complementing [[pdf_url]], which is the address
to send a download to.

The [[oa_status]] vocabulary is Unpaywall's and, as far as their data format
documents, always present.  We still guard against its absence with a
fallback derived from [[is_oa]], so a malformed record degrades to a coarse
open/closed answer rather than to [[None]]---which, on the [[Paper]] model,
would mean \enquote{never checked}.

<<oa normalization helpers>>=
def _normalize_oa(data: dict) -> dict:
    """Flatten an Unpaywall DOI object into the fields Scholar keeps."""
    is_oa = bool(data.get("is_oa"))
    best = data.get("best_oa_location") or {}
    pdf_url = best.get("url_for_pdf")
    if not pdf_url:
        for location in data.get("oa_locations") or []:
            if location.get("url_for_pdf"):
                pdf_url = location["url_for_pdf"]
                break
    return {
        "is_oa": is_oa,
        "oa_status": data.get("oa_status")
        or ("open" if is_oa else "closed"),
        "oa_url": best.get("url") or best.get("url_for_landing_page"),
        "pdf_url": pdf_url,
        "host_type": best.get("host_type"),
        "version": best.get("version"),
        "license": best.get("license"),
    }
@

<<test functions>>=
class TestNormalizeOA:
    """Tests for _normalize_oa fallbacks."""

    def test_pdf_falls_back_to_other_location(self):
        """When the best copy has no PDF link, another location's is used."""
        data = {
            "is_oa": True,
            "oa_status": "bronze",
            "best_oa_location": {
                "url": "https://publisher.example/landing",
                "url_for_pdf": None,
            },
            "oa_locations": [
                {"url_for_pdf": None},
                {"url_for_pdf": "https://repo.example/paper.pdf"},
            ],
        }
        result = _normalize_oa(data)
        assert result["pdf_url"] == "https://repo.example/paper.pdf"
        assert result["oa_url"] == "https://publisher.example/landing"

    def test_missing_status_degrades_to_open_or_closed(self):
        assert _normalize_oa({"is_oa": True})["oa_status"] == "open"
        assert _normalize_oa({})["oa_status"] == "closed"

    def test_empty_record_has_no_links(self):
        result = _normalize_oa({})
        assert result["pdf_url"] is None
        assert result["oa_url"] is None
        assert result["is_oa"] is False
